# Loop body reads an element an earlier iteration rewrote

Verifies the emitted loop body does not keep the element's first-iteration
subtype. The body adds `1mm` to `a[0]` before rewriting it as `2cm`, so the
second iteration must read the stored centimeter value: `20mm + 1mm = 21mm`.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm]

for (i in 0..2) {
    print(a[0] + 1mm)
    a[0] = 2cm
}

<<< stdout
11mm
21mm

<<< stderr
